[{:seon.task/name "a-failure-attaches-a-refinement"
  :seon.task/plan "Lane AGENTS (in flight). inv1: on any failed attempt the reconciler writes :seon.task/execution :held over the owner's release (:bail, reconcile.clj:366-384, :523-524; merge-train refusal :617-619), nothing re-releases it, and its dependents wait forever with no record. DECISIONS: nothing is held for release or relaunched; a failure attaches new tasks worked by new agents from the improved plan and the evidence. Attach a refinement chain until the task's declared budget (:seon.task/budget, replacing :max-attach) is spent."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/a-capped-attempt-attaches-a-refinement-not-a-hold}}
 {:seon.task/name "stuck-is-observed-data"
  :seon.task/plan "When the budget is spent the task is observed stuck: a derived :seon.task/stuck fact names the attempt, its cause and the tasks it blocks; problem class :stuck; the reconciler reports quiescence positively (:seon.root/quiescent). The harness (t5/src/t5/run.clj) and e2e end on quiescence and print the stuck rows: their time limits and settled? polling go (owner: a timeout that ends a run is a fence)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.reconcile/a-failure-attaches-a-refinement"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/a-spent-budget-is-a-stuck-fact-naming-what-it-blocks
                      seon.reconcile-test/quiescence-is-reported-when-nothing-can-move}}
 {:seon.task/name "contract-gaps-have-one-rule"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-10-21 by lane AGENTS: which contract gaps an attempt answers for is decided in three places. The turn loop takes harvest/uncontracted now minus the gaps when the attempt began (seon.turn/begin!, observe, turn.clj); root's judge takes the branch's program entries that have no contract and differ from main's (judge-tx, reconcile.clj:588-600); and before e37b318 the door's context read took every gap (it showed 400 seeded app.m*/f* gaps from seon.db's seed program as refusals). Two rules can disagree: a gap main gained after the branch point, or a var the agent re-evaluated unchanged. Correct: one function, the judge's (gaps on the branch's program entries that differ from main's base), called by the turn loop, the context and the judge alike. Deletes :gaps-before."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/the-loop-the-context-and-the-judge-name-the-same-gaps}}]
